  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Is a root canal painful?",
      "a": "Not at all. We use local anesthesia and advanced rotary technology so you won't feel pain during the procedure. Thoda sensitivity ho sakta hai baad me, jo 1-2 din me theek ho jayega."
    },
    {
      "q": "Do you offer EMI for dental implants?",
      "a": "Yes, we have 0% interest EMI options available through Bajaj Finserv for treatments above ₹20,000."
    },
    {
      "q": "How long does teeth whitening last?",
      "a": "Usually 1 to 3 years depending on your lifestyle. Tea, coffee, and smoking ka asar padta hai, so touch-ups are recommended."
    },
    {
      "q": "Do I need an appointment or can I walk in?",
      "a": "Prior appointment is highly recommended to avoid waiting, par dental emergencies like severe pain me walk-ins are accommodated immediately."
    },
    {
      "q": "Konsa insurance accept karte ho aap?",
      "a": "We accept most major corporate cashless policies including Star Health and HDFC Ergo. You can send your card details on WhatsApp to verify."
    },
    {
      "q": "How much do dental implants cost?",
      "a": "A single implant with crown starts from ₹18,000 per tooth. Final cost depends on bone condition and implant brand — use the cost estimator above or send your X-ray on WhatsApp for an exact quote."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I consult the doctor online first?",
      "a": "Yes. A video teleconsult on Google Meet costs ₹300 — ideal for a second opinion or to review your X-rays before visiting. Book it from the Teleconsult section."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I pay in instalments without a credit card?",
      "a": "Yes. No-cost EMI is available on debit cards and through finance partners for eligible treatments. KYC documents ready rakhein, approval 10 minutes me ho jaata hai."
    },
    {
      "q": "What are your clinic timings?",
      "a": "Monday to Friday 10 AM – 8 PM, Saturday 10 AM – 5 PM, with a 1 – 4 PM break every day. Sunday is closed. Live open/closed status is shown at the top of this page."
    },
    {
      "q": "What should I do in a dental emergency?",
      "a": "For severe pain, swelling or a knocked-out tooth, call the emergency number right away. Knocked-out tooth ko doodh me rakh kar 30 minute ke andar clinic aayein."
    },
    {
      "q": "Do you treat children?",
      "a": "Yes, we see children from 3 years onwards for check-ups, fillings, fluoride and sealants, in a calm, child-friendly setting."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do you ensure hygiene and sterilisation?",
      "a": "Every instrument goes through a Class B autoclave cycle and is sealed in a pouch that is opened in front of you. Disposables are single-use only."
    }
  ],
